      "hints": [
        "General term is $\\binom{5}{r} x^{5-r} (-\\frac{2}{x})^r = \\binom{5}{r}(-2)^r x^{5-2r}$.",
        "Set power $5 - 2r = -1 \\implies r = 3$.",
        "Evaluate $\\binom{5}{3}(-2)^3 = 10(-8) = -80$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Write the general term in the binomial expansion of $\\left(x - \\frac{2}{x}\\right)^5$:\n$$T_{r+1} = \\binom{5}{r} x^{5 - r} \\left(-\\frac{2}{x}\\right)^r = \\binom{5}{r} (-2)^r x^{5 - 2r}$$",
        "Set the power of $x$ to $-1$ to find the index $r$ for the term in $\\frac{1}{x}$:\n$$5 - 2r = -1 \\implies 2r = 6 \\implies r = 3$$",
        "Substitute $r = 3$ to calculate the coefficient:\n$$\\text{Term} = \\binom{5}{3} (-2)^3 x^{-1} = 10 \\times (-8) x^{-1} = -80x^{-1}$$\n$$\\text{Coefficient of } \\frac{1}{x} = -80$$"
      ],
